 # Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                                  
                                                                                                                     
 ## Introduction                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                                   
+                                                                                                                    
+## Recent Advances and Applications                                                                                 
+                                                                                                                    
+The field continues to expand into novel computational paradigms and practical implementations. Recent work proposes
**atom computing** as a successor to transistor-based architectures, suggesting that controlled flows of single      
electrons or photons could overcome current scaling limits by redefining matter and energy interactions              
[^10.34257_gjsfra257362]. In parallel, educational and simulation tools are bridging the gap between theory and      
practice, such as Python-based simulations of the BB84 quantum key distribution protocol that model state            
preparation, eavesdropping, and classical post-processing [^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724].                           
+                                                                                                                    
+Developer ecosystems and software engineering around quantum technologies are also maturing. An empirical analysis  
of developer discussions reveals that hybrid quantum-classical computing and circuit implementation dominate         
community engagement, with Qiskit and Q-sharp being the most referenced tools [^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427]. To
support this growing ecosystem, new hybrid iterative cipher chaining systems like CypherGliph have been benchmarked  
across classical, GPU/FPGA, and quantum computing platforms to evaluate post-quantum cryptographic resilience        
[^10.56975_tijer.v13i3.161368].                                                                                      
+                                                                                                                    
+## Quantum Cryptography and Security                                                                                
+                                                                                                                    
+Securing communications against future quantum threats remains a critical research vector. A new cryptographic      
approach details the implementation of BB84, B92, and B91 protocols alongside Shor's algorithm on quantum hardware to
enhance data security [^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406]. Concurrently, cryptanalysis research has introduced       
algorithmic improvements to dual lattice attacks against Learning With Errors (LWE), demonstrating that these attacks
can now exceed the efficiency of primal attacks and significantly reduce the estimated security levels of NIST       
post-quantum cryptography finalists like Kyber and Dilithium [^10.5281_zenodo.6493704].                              
+                                                                                                                    
+## Quantum Internet and Network Architectures                                                                       
+                                                                                                                    
+Beyond individual processors, the vision of a global quantum network is gaining theoretical traction. Recent primers
outline the foundational protocols for a quantum Internet, emphasizing its potential to provide ultra-secure         
connectivity and transform industries by transmitting information encoded in quantum states across distributed       
quantum devices [^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1]. Tracking the adoption and financial trends of such emerging technologies
is also becoming data-driven, with studies leveraging GitHub repositories and financial news to map quantum          
technology trajectories [^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20].                                                             
+                                                                                                                    
+## Quantum Simulation and Scientific Computing                                                                      
+                                                                                                                    
+Quantum computing is increasingly applied to complex scientific simulations. In computational fluid dynamics (CFD), 
researchers are exploring quantum algorithms based on the Lattice Boltzmann Method and Navier-Stokes equations to    
simulate 2D flows and aeronautical heat exchangers, marking an early but promising stage of development              
[^10.11159_icffts23.133][^10.21741_9781644902813-38]. Similarly, quantum annealing is being utilized for             
configurational analysis in materials science, providing a practical guide for calculating the relative energies of  
defective graphene structures [^10.1063_5.0151346]. Furthermore, open-source software like PULSEE leverages quantum  
simulation techniques to model nuclear magnetic resonance observables, bridging condensed matter physics and quantum 
information science [^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598].                                                                    
+                                                                                                                    
+## Quantum Algorithms and Optimization                                                                              
+                                                                                                                    
+Algorithmic efficiency on near-term quantum hardware is a major focus. Hybrid approaches combining granular         
computing with quantum processors have been developed to optimize continuous functions, allowing digital computers to
handle fitness evaluations while quantum devices evolve genetic populations [^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9].           
+                                                                                                                    
+## Historical Context and Architectural Comparisons                                                                 
+                                                                                                                    
+Foundational reviews continue to clarify the landscape. Early comparative studies have provided standardized        
architectural descriptions of digital, quantum, and biological computers to contextualize quantum performance        
potential [^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430]. Comprehensive overviews also continue to explore the core principles of        
superposition and entanglement, mapping out prospective applications and industry disruptions                        
[^10.5120_ijca2021921834].                                                                                           
                                                                                                                     

